'One complete static kitchen utensil rest arrangement, one new scene zero new independent models. One whole qualified deep-bowl long-hook ladle rests with its complete bowl underside on the left of a broad low deck while its original open upper return hook meets a slim supported cross rail. One whole qualified opaque tapered-tube and rounded-bulb baster lies separately at the right on the same complete deck. Exact source GLB buffers, normals, material dictionaries, face assignments and internal hierarchies remain unchanged under unit-scale translations only. The complete connected deck, two upright posts and narrow upper cross rail are new scene context only, not independently counted furniture or utensil models. This open high-and-low utensil rest is not the old colander-whisk backsplash counter with replaced props, a wall mirror ledge or a divided carry caddy. No parts cropped, rescaled, recoloured or recounted. Empty fixed game art only; no liquid, food-contact, real suction, serving, hook capacity, stability, working workflow, installation, manufacture or safety claim. Rigging animation and interaction not made.'
